-- title:
--   Krull dimension at most two for the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring in a universe $u$ which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and which is complete (and separated) for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, in the sense of `IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal W) W`. Let $\pi \in W$ be an irreducible element and let $E$ be a natural number with $1 \le E$. Form the ring of formal power series `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W$, and let `uvCrossingIdeal W (π ^ E)` be the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \pi^{E}$, where $\pi^{E}$ is viewed as a constant power series. The assertion is that the quotient ring `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)` $= W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{E})$ has Krull dimension at most $2$, the inequality being read in `WithBot ℕ∞`, the value group of `ringKrullDim`. The proof cites the statement that this quotient is a local domain which is integrally closed, and that it is a Noetherian ring.
--
--   This is the dimension bound for the local model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$ of a curve with a node over a complete discrete valuation ring; the maximal ideal is minimal over the two-element system $(\pi, U+V)$, so Krull's height theorem applies. It is used in the analysis of the node annulus, where it forces the non-maximal primes of the node ring to have height at most one, so that the relevant evaluation kernels localise to discrete valuation rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_ringKrullDim_le_two.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u
open ModularCurve ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel IsLocalRing in

theorem ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.ringKrullDim_le_two
    {W : Type u} [CommRing W] [IsDomain W] [IsDiscreteValuationRing W] [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal W) W]
    (π : W) (hπ : Irreducible π) (E : ℕ) (hE : 1 ≤ E) :
    ringKrullDim (UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)) ≤ 2 := by sorry
